    'sc.effBits': 'effective bits',
    'sc.bias': 'bias',
    'sc.curveNote': 'NRMSE is the root mean square error divided by the output range, over 512 pairs of uniform inputs. Effective bits: those of an ideal converter with the same error. With random bits the error falls as 1/√N: doubling the precision costs 4 times more cycles, and matching the 8 bit binary would take about {neq} bits. The Sobol sequence spreads the ones evenly and the error falls as 1/N{sob}. The LFSRs have period 255 and stop improving at N = 256; a single LFSR for all streams is very wrong at any N, because the streams become correlated.',
