    'sc.costNote': 'The operation itself is tiny ({op}), but each stream needs a generator (LFSR plus comparator) and the output needs a counter: they dominate the area. The stochastic circuit has {el} elements (gates and flip flops) against {bin} gates of the binary one, but it works for {N} cycles: the estimated energy (every element active in every cycle) is {r} times that of the binary circuit. Stochastic computing pays off when generators are shared, when values already arrive as streams (from sensors, for instance) or when fault tolerance matters more than energy.',
    'sc.faultSc': 'stochastic NRMSE ({gen}, N = {N})',
