    'hls.langTitle': 'Language and directives',
    'hls.langHelp': '<p>A subset of C: types <code>u8 u16 u32 i8 i16 i32</code> (and <code>int</code>, <code>uint8_t</code> ...), 1 or 2 dimensional arrays in the parameters (the kernel memories), <code>#define</code>, <code>const</code> tables, <code>for</code> with constant bounds and an optional label, assignments, <code>?:</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>max</code> and <code>abs</code>. Division and remainder only by a power of 2, shifts only by a constant; there is no <code>if</code> or <code>while</code>.</p><p>Directives, as in Vitis HLS: <code>#pragma HLS pipeline II=n</code> (unrolls the inner loops), <code>#pragma HLS unroll</code> or <code>unroll factor=n</code>, <code>#pragma HLS array_partition variable=v type=cyclic|block|complete factor=n dim=d</code> and <code>#pragma HLS allocation operation instances=mul|add limit=n</code>.</p><p>The width of each operation comes from value range analysis (not only from the type): it picks the 8 or 16 bit multiplier and the 8, 16 or 32 bit adder of the synthesized library.</p>',
