    'hls.lineN': 'line {n}',
    'hls.modelNotes': '<p>Estimate before synthesis, like that of an HLS tool, calibrated against Vitis HLS and Vivado 2022.2 (results/vitis): the delay, area and energy of each unit come from the sky130 synthesis (unit library), LUT and CARRY4 from the FPGA synthesis; multiplexers, comparators, logic and registers (dfxtp_1: {reg} µm², clock to output {cq} ps, setup {su} ps, {ereg} fJ per cycle) were measured with the same flow.</p><ul><li>Chaining: operations fit in a cycle while their summed delays do not exceed the period minus {cq} + {su} ps; the delay of the input multiplexers is not considered in scheduling.</li><li>Synchronous memory: read latency of {mem} cycle; each bank has the chosen ports; with a pipeline, the address computation is counted in LUTs; a partition factor that is not a power of 2 costs a division by a constant per index and a remainder (urem) that adds latency; memory area and energy are not counted.</li><li>Loop without pipeline: {loop} control cycle per iteration plus {sub} per inner loop; with a pipeline: {pipe} entry cycle, latency = depth + (N − 1) II; a loop without pipeline that only contains a pipelined loop is flattened, as in Vitis (rows_cols).</li><li>The same rule for exact and approximate units: adders and multiplications by a constant (the exact ones become shift and add) are not shared; multiplications between variables are, when the shared instances with their multiplexers cost less than one unit per operation. An adder truncated by k bits costs the exact adder of the same width in the ratio (W − k)/W (the low bits are wires). The cost of each instance comes from the netlist after constant propagation (constant operands, high bits known zero from the range).</li><li>Energy per run: energy per operation of the units (uniform inputs), registers in every cycle (no clock gating) and leakage; without the clock tree.</li><li>Value ranges by interval analysis (conservative): the chosen width may be larger than needed.</li></ul>',
    'hls.segInfo': '{depth} cycles per run, {execs} runs; useful cycle time {tc} ps (register {ov} ps)',
